#first open visual studio code 
  ###in the terminal run terraform destroy
  #click on the vpc.tf file delete everything copy from line 5 till 10 and change my name to your name
  # Create a VPC
resource "aws_vpc" "projecty-vpc" { #the name of the refrence block is projecty-vpc custom naming convention
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  tags = {
    Name = "gopal-vpc"
  }
}
###do terraform apply
  1. go to aws console search vpc and check the vpc is created or not. 
  2. copy the vpc id
  3. open terraform.tfstate file go extreme below you will find the id which contains vpc id match it witht he vpc id you got it from console of aws. 
  4. inside the state file check the vpc with refrence block name 

  ###next we will add subnet 
  ##add this subnet block from line number 19 till 27
  resource "aws_subnet" "projecty-subnet" {
  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.projecty-vpc.id #this subnet need to be mapped with your vpc
  #aws_vpc.projecty-vpc.id #this line should contains the vpc id which is created earlier
  #terraform apply : it will read all your manifest file and compare with your state file 
  cidr_block = "10.0.1.0/24"
  tags = {
    Name = "gopal-subnet"
  }
}

#####activity need to done
1. terraform plan
  2. terraform plan will show the vpc id. if you look into line 20 then open the state file there you will see the mapping of aws_vpc.refblock.atheendid
  3. terraform apply ##this will also show that it is picking up the vpc id but it is picking up from your state file
  4. verify finally from aws console go to subnet you will see the subnet iis created and mapped with your vpc
